F]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]1[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] wave[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]backlog_batch_b6.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/backlog_batch_b6.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim] Parent: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/backlog_batch_b5.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-dw[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-dw/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Expose RecoveryAssessment for failed-close snapshot imports[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]recovery-assessment-public[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]recovery-assessment-public: resolve bob-cli-dt in sase by exposing the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared failed-close assessment type through a public name and updating [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]_failed_close_recovery_snapshots.py (and any other consumers) to import [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that public name. Do not suppress, whitelist, or pragma the private [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]_RecoveryAssessment misuse. Read SASE symvision policy first. Verify [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with focused failed-close snapshot/recovery tests plus sase tool run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]check in the opened sase checkout. Independent clean witness [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]13ea2a464abef73b3eab4bfee9e624d7 already makes this KNOWN; later checks [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]including 5d1634e22bc172fe358db97b9279961f still report it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the LSP store identity-lock wait test contend [/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]deterministically[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]lsp-store-lock-flake[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]lsp-store-lock-flake: resolve bob-cli-dv in sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests/test_sase_core_wheel_cache_tool.py::test_lsp_store_rechecks_after_[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]waiting_for_identity_lock. The node failed under parallel scoped load of[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SASE check 5d1634e22bc172fe358db97b9279961f (AssertionError: Waiting for[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the shared build lock in empty stderr) and passed 3/3 isolated reruns on[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the same tree (d79366e7627ad5290e34d797cb5c6a7a, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]f02021819c78b654a26d3739e330ddeb, 6d94f3e4d28d96bbaf830bde9189b048). [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Root cause: FAKE_CARGO_DELAY=0.3 plus a 5s marker poll lets the first [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fake cargo finish before the second store contends. Hold the first [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]process in cargo until the second is observed, or otherwise make the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lock wait deterministic. Do not suppress the node. Verify with focused [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]serial and parallel reruns plus sase tool run check.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Restore the unconfigured-theme caret-underline XCTests on [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]macOS CI[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-unconfigured-theme-ci[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-unconfigured-theme-ci: resolve bob-cli-dr in bob-mac-capture. Master[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]macOS 26 SwiftPM Test has failed on every push since 8b57693 with the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]same four assertions in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]CapturePanelModelTests.testCaretLeavingUnconfiguredThemeUnderlinesAfterA[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]nalysis and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]CaptureUnconfiguredThemeHostedTests.testTypingUnconfiguredThemeThenMovin[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gCaretUnderlinesWithoutFreezing (timeout then XCTAssertTrue at th